# The fixture filesystem dcheck's and ncheck's b6sim cases walk -- task C4e.
#
# WHY THIS IS NOT ../../df/test/fsimg.img.  Two reasons, and the second is the harder one.
# df's fixture has no HARD LINK, so every link count on it is 1 and dcheck could only ever
# be wrong in one direction; it has no device node and no setuid file, so `ncheck -s' --
# whose whole job is to find those two -- would have nothing to report; and nothing on it is
# nested more than one level, so ncheck's pname() would never recurse.  And cmd/dcheck is
# configured BEFORE cmd/df (`dcheck' sorts ahead of `dd' and `df'), so its test directory
# cannot depend on df_fsimg at all.  ../../ncheck/test copies this one rather than building
# a third, which is the arrangement ../../quot/test has with df's.
#
# WHAT EACH ENTRY IS FOR.  Nothing here is decoration:
#
#   /f + /flink   one inode with TWO names, so a link count above 1 exists to be right
#                 about -- and so ncheck prints one i-number twice, which is the thing that
#                 makes an i-number-to-name listing interesting rather than a permutation.
#   /d/e/g        three levels, so ncheck's pname() recurses and dcheck walks a directory
#                 that is not the root.
#   /setuid       mode 04755, one of the two things `ncheck -s' looks for.
#   /dev/tty      a character special, the other one.  di_addr[0] is the device number
#                 there rather than a block address, which is why dcheck and ncheck look at
#                 di_mode before they look at anything else.
#
# 100 blocks and a fixed timestamp, for ../../df/test/fsimg.manifest's reason: the image
# must be byte-reproducible or a count is not an expectation.  The `source' paths resolve
# against b6fsutil's working directory, which is this test's build directory.

default
owner 0
group 0
dirmode 0755
filemode 0644

dir /d
dir /d/e
dir /dev

file /f
source dcheckimg.d/small

link /flink
target /f

file /d/e/g
source dcheckimg.d/small

file /setuid
mode 04755
source dcheckimg.d/small

cdev /dev/tty
major 5
minor 0
mode 0620
